roduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/learn/introduction#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"105":{"id":"/docs/learn/introduction-6","page_id":"/docs/learn/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/learn/introduction","content":"CForge is a **backend DSL and systems-language experiment** (release 0.1). The runnable piece is a tiny typed language plus a **C runtime** that owns networking, HTTP, TLS, JSON parsing, and storage — handlers express policy; the runtime owns mechanism."},"106":{"id":"/docs/learn/introduction-7","page_id":"/docs/learn/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/learn/introduction","content":"We are **not** claiming memory safety like Rust: `Slice`/`Ctx` lifetime rules are documented and partially checked, but **`@safe` is not enforced yet**. See Safety modes."},"107":{"id":"/docs/learn/introduction-8","page_id":"/docs/learn/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/learn/introduction#what-we-optimize-for-direction-c","content":"A **backend systems niche**: small handler code, predictable request memory (arenas + slabs), integer error codes, and a stable `int32_t handler(Ctx *)` ABI — not a full general-purpose language yet."},"108":{"id":"/docs/learn/introduction-9","page_id":"/docs/learn/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/learn/introduction#design-principles","content":"**No hidden work** — allocation, syscalls, and buffer lifetimes are visible."},"109":{"id":"/docs/learn/introduction-10","page_id":"/docs/learn/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/learn/introduction#design-principles","content":"**Libraries, not language features** — HTTP, JSON, TLS, and SQL are runtime code you link, not syntax built into the compiler."},"110":{"id":"/docs/learn/introduction-11","page_id":"/docs/learn/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/learn/introduction#design-principles","content":"**Two backends** — rapid iteration through C codegen; native ELF for registers and syscalls on x86-64."},"111":{"id":"/docs/learn/introduction-12","page_id":"/docs/learn/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/learn/introduction#design-principles","content":"**Explicit memory** — connection buffers, request arenas, and `Slice` views; reset arenas per request instead of GC."},"112":{"id":"/docs/learn/introduction-13","page_id":"/docs/learn/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/learn/introduction#what-cforge-is-not","content":"CForge is **not** a memory-safe language like Rust. It does **not** replace PostgreSQL, Kubernetes, or a full package ecosystem in release 0.1. See Implementation status for the exact matrix."},"113":{"id":"/docs/learn/introduction-14","page_id":"/docs/learn/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/learn/introduction#architecture","content":"The machine backend bypasses C codegen for small programs and emits ELF directly."},"114":{"id":"/docs/learn/introduction-15","page_id":"/docs/learn/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/learn/introduction#comparison","content":"CForge"},"115":{"id":"/docs/learn/introduction-16","page_id":"/docs/learn/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/learn/introduction#comparison","content":"C"},"116":{"id":"/docs/learn/introduction-17","page_id":"/docs/learn/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/learn/introduction#comparison","content":"Rust"},"117":{"id":"/docs/learn/introduction-18","page_id":"/docs/learn/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/learn/introduction#comparison","content":"Control"},"118":{"id":"/docs/learn/introduction-19","page_id":"/docs/learn/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/learn/introduction#comparison","content":"High"},"119":{"id":"/docs/learn/introduction-20","page_id":"/docs/learn/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/learn/introduction#comparison","content":"High"},"120":{"id":"/docs/learn/introduction-21","page_id":"/docs/learn/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","u