nt":"Error and control-flow policy"},"466":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-4","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/boundary#route-registration-abi","content":"Route registration ABI"},"467":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-5","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/boundary#ffi-c-runtime-and-foreign-libraries","content":"FFI: C runtime and foreign libraries"},"468":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-6","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/boundary#machine-backend-boundary","content":"Machine backend boundary"},"469":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-7","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/boundary#anti-patterns-at-the-boundary","content":"Anti-patterns at the boundary"},"470":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-8","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/boundary#summary","content":"Summary"},"471":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-9","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary","content":"The CForge backend ecosystem depends on a **hard boundary** between what the `.cforge` compiler understands and what the linked runtime provides. This separation keeps the language small, makes the runtime replaceable, and allows the same handler source to target generated C or (eventually) native code with identical ABI symbols."},"472":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-10","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-language-owns","content":"**Shipped (0.1):** The `cforge` driver lexes and parses a statement-oriented subset: functions, `let`, `if`/`while`, `return`, and calls. Types map directly to C11 scalars and two runtime-visible structs:"},"473":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-11","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-language-owns","content":"CForge type"},"474":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-12","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-language-owns","content":"ABI shape"},"475":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-13","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-language-owns","content":"`i32`, `u32`, `i64`, `u64`, `u16`, `u8`, `bool`"},"476":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-14","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-language-owns","content":"Fixed-width integers / `int32_t` for `bool`"},"477":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-15","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-language-owns","content":"`Slice`"},"478":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-16","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-language-owns","content":"`{ uint8_t *ptr; size_t len; }`"},"479":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-17","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-language-owns","content":"`*Ctx`"},"480":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-18","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-language-owns","content":"Opaque request context"},"481":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-19","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-language-owns","content":"`*u64`, `*u32`, `*Slice`"},"482":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-20","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-language-owns","content":"Out-parameters and mutable views"},"483":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-21","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-language-owns","content":"`Slice` is a **non-owning view**. Copying a `Slice` copies pointer and length only. String literals become static `Slice` values pointing at read-only bytes. Handlers must not retain `Slice` pointers past the request unless documentation guarantees a longer lifetime (database helpers copy into the request arena for this reason)."},"484":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-22","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-language-owns","content":"The entry `main` lowers to `cforge_main`; the generated translation unit adds a C `main` that registers routes and calls `app_listen`. Application functions are `static` in the generated file and passed as `CForgeFn` pointers."},"485":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-23","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-language-owns","content":"**Planned:** `struct` declarations at module scope, generics for containers, `async fn` with state-machine lowering, and comptime validation of route tables. None of these change the rule that **syscalls and protocol parsing stay out of the language**."},"486":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-24","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-runtime-owns","content":"Everything that touches the outside world:"},"487":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-25","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-runtime-owns","content":"Socket creation, `bind`, `listen`, `accept4`, non-blocking mode, `TCP_NODELAY`, keep-alive"},"488":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-26","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-runtime-owns","content":"`epoll_wait` loop, connection slot table, idle scanning, accept pause under load"},"489":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-27","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-runtime-owns","content":"HTTP request parsing, response framing, status codes, `Allow` headers"},"490":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-28","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-runtime-owns","content":"TLS 1.3 handshake and record I/O via OpenSSL"},"491":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-29","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-runtime-owns","content":"JSON parsers and response encoders scoped to known schemas"},"492":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-30","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-runtime-owns","content":"SQLite connection, prepared statements, WAL pragmas, busy timeout"},"493":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-31","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-runtime-owns","content":"Environment-based configuration (`PORT`, `CFORGE_DB`, TLS paths, limits)"},"494":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-32","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-runtime-owns","content":"Process signals, graceful shutdown, stderr logging"},"495":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-33","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#what-the-runtime-owns","content":"Application code chooses **which routes exist** and **which status codes and DB calls** to make. It does not choose buffer sizes, epoll user-data encoding, or SSL context flags."},"496":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-34","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#the-ctx-contract","content":"`Ctx` is stack-allocated per request inside the runtime. Handlers receive `*Ctx` only. Fields visible through API functions include:"},"497":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-35","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#the-ctx-contract","content":"HTTP method and path as `Slice` (path without query string for routing)"},"498":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-36","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#the-ctx-contract","content":"Request body as `Slice` (bounded by `CFORGE_MAX_BODY`)"},"499":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-37","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#the-ctx-contract","content":"Output buffer cursor managed by `ctx_text`, `ctx_json_*`, `ctx_status`"},"500":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-38","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#the-ctx-contract","content":"Up to four captured path parameters (`:id` style), parsed via `ctx_param_u64`"},"501":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-39","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#the-ctx-contract","content":"Handlers must not store `Ctx` pointers beyond the synchronous return of `CForgeFn`. **Planned** async models may extend `Ctx` with a generation token or arena id so resumed tasks cannot write into recycled slots."},"502":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-40","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#error-and-control-flow-policy","content":"There is no exception unwinding. Functions return `int32_t`:"},"503":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-41","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#error-and-control-flow-policy","content":"Pattern"},"504":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-42","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#error-and-control-flow-policy","content":"Meaning"},"505":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-43","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#error-and-control-flow-policy","content":"`0`"},"506":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-44","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#error-and-control-flow-policy","content":"Success"},"507":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-45","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#error-and-control-flow-policy","content":"`1`"},"508":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-46","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#error-and-control-flow-policy","content":"Expected domain miss (e.g. row not found)"},"509":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-47","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#error-and-control-flow-policy","content":"`-1`"},"510":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-48","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#error-and-control-flow-policy","content":"Parse failure, I/O error, constraint violation"},"511":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-49","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#error-and-control-flow-policy","content":"HTTP mapping is application responsibility: `404` for missing users, `400` for bad JSON, `503` when `db_*` returns `-1`. The runtime may emit its own `400`/`413`/`431` before a handler runs when HTTP is malformed."},"512":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-50","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#error-and-control-flow-policy","content":"This policy keeps generated C simple and makes FFI predictable: every exported runtime function uses the same width and sign convention."},"513":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-51","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#route-registration-abi","content":"Before `app_listen`, the generated `cforge_main` calls:"},"514":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-52","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#route-registration-abi","content":"Paths are copied at registration time (malloc at startup only). Lookup at request time is linear scan with exact match or single trailing `:param` segment—**Shipped (0.1)**. **Planned:** radix tree or perfect hash for large tables, method bitmaps per path, middleware chains stored as function pointer arrays."},"515":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-53","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#route-registration-abi","content":"Handlers have type `int32_t (*)(Ctx *)`. The runtime never calls back into the language except through this pointer."},"516":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-54","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#ffi-c-runtime-and-foreign-libraries","content":"**Today:** Generated C includes `cforge_rt.h` and links `server.c`, `json.c`, `db.c` with `libsqlite3`, `libssl`, `libcrypto`, `pthread`. New runtime capabilities are added as C functions and whitelisted in the compiler’s builtin call table."},"517":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-55","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#ffi-c-runtime-and-foreign-libraries","content":"**Planned FFI layers:**"},"518":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-56","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#ffi-c-runtime-and-foreign-libraries","content":"**Stable C ABI** — `CFORGE_API` functions documented in reference; versioned struct sizes for `Ctx` extensions."},"519":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-57","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#ffi-c-runtime-and-foreign-libraries","content":"**Dynamic plugins** — `.so` loaded at startup registering routes or background jobs (explicit opt-in; no runtime `dlopen` in 0.1)."},"520":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-58","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#ffi-c-runtime-and-foreign-libraries","content":"**Foreign DB/cache clients** — PostgreSQL libpq or custom wire codec in C++; handlers still see `db_*`-style integers."},"521":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-59","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#ffi-c-runtime-and-foreign-libraries","content":"**Rust or Zig shims** — thin wrappers exporting `extern \"C\"` symbols matching `CForgeFn` and allocator rules."},"522":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-60","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#ffi-c-runtime-and-foreign-libraries","content":"FFI code must respect **arena lifetimes**: any `Slice` handed to a handler must either point at static data, connection `in[]`, or the request arena until reset."},"523":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-61","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#machine-backend-boundary","content":"The machine backend compiles a different subset to x86-64 ELF without linking the HTTP runtime. Registers `r0`–`r7` map to System V argument registers. Syscalls are explicit. There is no `Ctx` or `app_listen` on this path—it proves the front-end can target non-C ABIs."},"524":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-62","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#machine-backend-boundary","content":"Long-term, shared middle-end IR would feed both C codegen and machine codegen; handlers for microservices remain on the C server path until the IR backend can link a minimal runtime."},"525":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-63","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#anti-patterns-at-the-boundary","content":"Parsing HTTP or SQL in `.cforge` — duplicates runtime, breaks size limits."},"526":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-64","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#anti-patterns-at-the-boundary","content":"Calling `malloc` from handlers — violates allocation invariants; use runtime helpers that draw from the arena."},"527":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-65","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#anti-patterns-at-the-boundary","content":"Holding `Slice` from `db_get_user` after return — use-before-free when the arena resets."},"528":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-66","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#anti-patterns-at-the-boundary","content":"Blocking syscalls in handlers — stalls the single-threaded epoll loop in 0.1; **planned** worker pool offloads such calls."},"529":{"id":"/docs/spec/boundary-67","page_id":"/docs/spec/boundary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/boundary#summary","content":"The boundary is intentional: **express policy in CForge, express mechanism in C**. Extending the ecosystem means growing `cforge_rt.h` and keeping the language dumb about wire formats. See http-async.html for protocol layer detail and memory.html for ownership rules."},"530":{"id":"/docs/spec/database","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","type":"page","content":"Database, pooling, cache, and message queues","breadcrumbs":["CForge","Specification"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/database"},"531":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-0","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"SQLite (shipped)"},"532":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-1","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/database#connection-pool-postgresql--mysql-target","content":"Connection pool (PostgreSQL / MySQL target)"},"533":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-2","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/database#postgresql-wire-client","content":"PostgreSQL wire client"},"534":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-3","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/database#transaction-boundaries","content":"Transaction boundaries"},"535":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-4","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/database#in-memory-and-distributed-cache","content":"In-memory and distributed cache"},"536":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-5","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/database#message-queues-planned","content":"Message queues (planned)"},"537":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-6","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/database#read-replicas-and-routing","content":"Read replicas and routing"},"538":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-7","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/database#backup-and-migrations","content":"Backup and migrations"},"539":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-8","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/database#security","content":"Security"},"540":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-9","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/database#01-vs-target-summary","content":"0.1 vs target summary"},"541":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-10","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database","content":"Persistence and asynchronous messaging in the CForge ecosystem are **runtime libraries**, not language builtins. Release 0.1 ships SQLite for the users service; this spec defines the target architecture for connection pools, external databases, in-memory cache, and queue integrations."},"542":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-11","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"**Shipped (0.1):** SQLite pool (`CFORGE_DB_POOL`, default 4) of connections with prepared statements. Same schema:"},"543":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-12","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"Pragmas at open: `journal_mode=WAL`, `synchronous=NORMAL`. Three prepared statements:"},"544":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-13","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"Parameters are bound; SQL text is never concatenated with user input. `SQLITE_TRANSIENT` on insert copies name bytes out of the request arena. `SELECT` copies TEXT into the arena before `sqlite3_reset`."},"545":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-14","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"**Checkout discipline:** Each `db_*` call checks out a pool connection. After the handler returns, `cforge_db_release` returns it to the pool and resets statements."},"546":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-15","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"**Optional Postgres:** When `CFORGE_PG_DSN` is set and the binary is built with libpq, the same `db_*` API uses PostgreSQL (`users` table, `BIGSERIAL` id). Metrics report `db_backend postgres` or `sqlite`."},"547":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-16","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"**Optional Redis:** When `CFORGE_REDIS_URL` is set, the runtime connects and `DEL user:{id}` on insert/delete (cache invalidation). Metrics report `redis_backend connected` or `disabled`."},"548":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-17","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"Integer API:"},"549":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-18","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"Return"},"550":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-19","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"Meaning"},"551":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-20","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"`0`"},"552":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-21","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"Success"},"553":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-22","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"`1`"},"554":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-23","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"Row missing (`GET`/`DELETE`)"},"555":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-24","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"`-1`"},"556":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-25","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"SQLite or bind error"},"557":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-26","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"Handlers map `-1` to `503` and increment `db_errors` in metrics."},"558":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-27","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#sqlite-shipped","content":"`busy_timeout` is 1000 ms for contention with external tools opening the same file."},"559":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-28","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#connection-pool-postgresql--mysql-target","content":"Target shape for additional pool features on Postgres:"},"560":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-29","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#connection-pool-postgresql--mysql-target","content":"Rules:"},"561":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-30","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#connection-pool-postgresql--mysql-target","content":"**Never** hold a pooled connection across `async` yield unless Model B explicitly pins conn to continuation"},"562":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-31","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#connection-pool-postgresql--mysql-target","content":"One statement cache per connection; reset on release"},"563":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-32","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#connection-pool-postgresql--mysql-target","content":"Health check query on idle timeout"},"564":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-33","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#connection-pool-postgresql--mysql-target","content":"Metrics: `pool_wait_ms`, `pool_active`, `pool_idle`, `pool_create_failures`"},"565":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-34","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#connection-pool-postgresql--mysql-target","content":"Handlers keep the integer error policy; `db_get_user` becomes a thin wrapper over `SELECT` with dialect-specific types. Migrations run from toolchain (`cforge migrate`) applying versioned SQL files—not from handlers."},"566":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-35","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#postgresql-wire-client","content":"**Shipped:** libpq via `CFORGE_PG_DSN` on the reactor thread (same sync model as 0.1)."},"567":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-36","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#postgresql-wire-client","content":"Design options for future scaling:"},"568":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-37","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#postgresql-wire-client","content":"Approach"},"569":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-38","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#postgresql-wire-client","content":"Pros"},"570":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-39","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#postgresql-wire-client","content":"Cons"},"571":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-40","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#postgresql-wire-client","content":"libpq"},"572":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-41","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#postgresql-wire-client","content":"Battle-tested, TLS built-in"},"573":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-42","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#postgresql-wire-client","content":"C dependency, blocking API"},"574":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-43","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#postgresql-wire-client","content":"Custom frontend/backend protocol"},"575":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-44","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#postgresql-wire-client","content":"Full control"},"576":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-45","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#postgresql-wire-client","content":"Large implementation"},"577":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-46","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#postgresql-wire-client","content":"Embedded via CGO/Rust shim"},"578":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-47","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#postgresql-wire-client","content":"Reuse ecosystem"},"579":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-48","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#postgresql-wire-client","content":"FFI boundary discipline"},"580":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-49","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#postgresql-wire-client","content":"CForge favors **libpq in worker threads** under Model B, with results marshaled into arena `Slice` on the reactor thread before handler return in hybrid mode."},"581":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-50","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#transaction-boundaries","content":"**0.1:** Each statement auto-commits. **Planned:** `db_tx_begin(ctx)` / `db_tx_commit` / `db_tx_rollback` storing tx state in `Ctx` extensions, forbidden across keep-alive requests unless explicitly bound to a session id."},"582":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-51","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#transaction-boundaries","content":"Isolation default: `READ COMMITTED` for OLTP handlers; serializable for financial slices via opt-in."},"583":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-52","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#in-memory-and-distributed-cache","content":"Layers:"},"584":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-53","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#in-memory-and-distributed-cache","content":"**Request arena** — not a cache; discard every request"},"585":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-54","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#in-memory-and-distributed-cache","content":"**Process LRU** — fixed-size slab for hot keys (user by id, JWKS)"},"586":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-55","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#in-memory-and-distributed-cache","content":"**Redis** — shared cache and rate-limit counters"},"587":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-56","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#in-memory-and-distributed-cache","content":"**CDN** — HTTP cache headers for static content"},"588":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-57","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#in-memory-and-distributed-cache","content":"Cache API sketch:"},"589":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-58","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#in-memory-and-distributed-cache","content":"Serialization format for values is caller-chosen (JSON blob, msgpack). **Stampede protection:** single-flight lock per key in process LRU; Redis `SET NX` for cross-node."},"590":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-59","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#in-memory-and-distributed-cache","content":"Invalidation: explicit `cache_del` on write paths (`POST`/`DELETE` users); **shipped** Redis `DEL user:{id}` when `CFORGE_REDIS_URL` is set; **planned** pub/sub channel `cache:invalidate` for multi-instance deployments."},"591":{"id":"/docs/spec/database-60","page_id":"/docs/spec/database","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/database#message-queues-planned","content":"Use cases: outbox pattern for email, audit log ship