ge_id":"/docs/spec/http-async","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/http-async#async-model-b--executor-and-continuations-planned","content":"Hybrid deployments may run Model A on edge nodes and Model B behind internal load balancers."},"746":{"id":"/docs/spec/http-async-107","page_id":"/docs/spec/http-async","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/http-async#websockets-and-sse-planned","content":"WebSocket upgrade would share the HTTP parser’s header phase, then switch slot mode to frame codec. Server-Sent Events reuse HTTP/1.1 chunked responses with `text/event-stream`. Both stay out of language syntax; registration resembles `app_get` with a protocol flag."},"747":{"id":"/docs/spec/http-async-108","page_id":"/docs/spec/http-async","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/http-async#websockets-and-sse-planned","content":"**Shipped:** `GET /ws` performs an RFC 6455 handshake and echoes client text frames (runtime-built; not registered via `app_get`)."},"748":{"id":"/docs/spec/http-async-109","page_id":"/docs/spec/http-async","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/http-async#caching-semantics-at-http-layer","content":"`ETag` / `If-None-Match` and `Cache-Control` for static assets are **planned**. Dynamic JSON APIs default to `Cache-Control: no-store` unless handlers set headers via future `ctx_header` API."},"749":{"id":"/docs/spec/http-async-110","page_id":"/docs/spec/http-async","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/http-async#error-responses","content":"Runtime-generated errors use fixed bodies or empty bodies per status. Application errors use `ctx_text` / `ctx_status`. **Shipped:** `ctx_problem` returns Problem Details (`application/problem+json`) with `title`, `detail`, and `status` fields (used on invalid create-user JSON)."},"750":{"id":"/docs/spec/http-async-111","page_id":"/docs/spec/http-async","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/http-async#testing-implications","content":"Integration tests in `./cforge test` cover pipelining, split header writes, TLS 1.3, WebSocket `/ws` echo, and graceful `SIGTERM`. Async Model B will need stress tests for continuation leaks and ordered response writes on one connection."},"751":{"id":"/docs/spec/http-async-112","page_id":"/docs/spec/http-async","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/http-async#testing-implications","content":"See networking.html for sockets and memory.html for buffer lifetimes during pipelining."},"752":{"id":"/docs/spec","page_id":"/docs/spec","type":"page","content":"CForge backend ecosystem specification","breadcrumbs":["CForge","Specification"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec"},"753":{"id":"/docs/spec-0","page_id":"/docs/spec","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec#architectural-stance","content":"Architectural stance"},"754":{"id":"/docs/spec-1","page_id":"/docs/spec","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec#layer-diagram","content":"Layer diagram"},"755":{"id":"/docs/spec-2","page_id":"/docs/spec","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec#request-lifecycle-reference-server","content":"Request lifecycle (reference server)"},"756":{"id":"/docs/spec-3","page_id":"/docs/spec","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec#specification-map","content":"Specification map"},"757":{"id":"/docs/spec-4","page_id":"/docs/spec","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec#design-invariants","content":"Design invariants"},"758":{"id":"/docs/spec-5","page_id":"/docs/spec","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec#relationship-to-other-docs","content":"Relationship to other docs"},"759":{"id":"/docs/spec-6","page_id":"/docs/spec","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec#versioning","content":"Versioning"},"760":{"id":"/docs/spec-7","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec","content":"This document set describes the **full CForge backend ecosystem design**: how application code, the language compiler, the C runtime, optional native machine code, and Linux facilities fit together to build network services. It is normative for **intent** and descriptive for **release 0.1**, which implements a vertical slice (HTTP/1.1, WebSocket `/ws`, SQLite pool, optional Postgres/Redis, TLS 1.3, single-threaded epoll) documented in the repository’s end-to-end guide."},"761":{"id":"/docs/spec-8","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec","content":"The specification is organized by concern, not by source file. Cross-cutting themes—explicit memory, integer error codes, library-not-language features, and predictable syscall budgets—appear in every layer."},"762":{"id":"/docs/spec-9","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#architectural-stance","content":"CForge targets **low-latency, allocation-bounded request paths** on Linux. The language expresses control flow and calls into a **stable runtime ABI** (`Slice`, `Ctx`, route registration, database helpers). The runtime owns syscalls, protocol state machines, buffer pools, and cryptographic primitives. There is no mandatory garbage collector and no hidden thread pool on the hot path in the reference server architecture."},"763":{"id":"/docs/spec-10","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#architectural-stance","content":"Three compile-time backends coexist in the long-term design:"},"764":{"id":"/docs/spec-11","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#architectural-stance","content":"Backend"},"765":{"id":"/docs/spec-12","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#architectural-stance","content":"Role"},"766":{"id":"/docs/spec-13","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#architectural-stance","content":"Typical artifact"},"767":{"id":"/docs/spec-14","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#architectural-stance","content":"**C server**"},"768":{"id":"/docs/spec-15","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#architectural-stance","content":"Fast iteration, full runtime link"},"769":{"id":"/docs/spec-16","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#architectural-stance","content":"`build/cforge-users` via generated C11"},"770":{"id":"/docs/spec-17","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#architectural-stance","content":"**Native machine**"},"771":{"id":"/docs/spec-18","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#architectural-stance","content":"Syscalls, tight loops, teaching"},"772":{"id":"/docs/spec-19","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#architectural-stance","content":"x86-64 ELF from `cforge_mach.py`"},"773":{"id":"/docs/spec-20","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#architectural-stance","content":"**Future IR**"},"774":{"id":"/docs/spec-21","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#architectural-stance","content":"Shared optimizations, cross-target"},"775":{"id":"/docs/spec-22","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#architectural-stance","content":"SSA-like IR lowering to C or machine"},"776":{"id":"/docs/spec-23","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#architectural-stance","content":"Release 0.1 ships the C server path and a partial machine path. The IR backend is roadmap only; see toolchain.html."},"777":{"id":"/docs/spec-24","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#layer-diagram","content":"Handlers never see file descriptors. The runtime passes **views** (`Slice`) into fixed per-connection storage. That boundary is the primary safety and performance contract; see boundary.html."},"778":{"id":"/docs/spec-25","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#request-lifecycle-reference-server","content":"A single client request on the 0.1 server traverses:"},"779":{"id":"/docs/spec-26","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#request-lifecycle-reference-server","content":"Future designs add HTTP/2 streams, async I/O variants, and worker threads without changing the handler signature; work is scheduled before `CForgeFn` is invoked. Details live in http-async.html and networking.html."},"780":{"id":"/docs/spec-27","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#specification-map","content":"Document"},"781":{"id":"/docs/spec-28","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#specification-map","content":"Topics"},"782":{"id":"/docs/spec-29","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#specification-map","content":"boundary.html"},"783":{"id":"/docs/spec-30","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#specification-map","content":"Language vs runtime, `Slice`/`Ctx`, error policy, FFI to C and native"},"784":{"id":"/docs/spec-31","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#specification-map","content":"networking.html"},"785":{"id":"/docs/spec-32","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#specification-map","content":"TCP/UDP, epoll, backpressure, TLS transport, DNS hooks"},"786":{"id":"/docs/spec-33","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#specification-map","content":"http-async.html"},"787":{"id":"/docs/spec-34","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#specification-map","content":"HTTP versions, router, JSON/serialization, async model A vs B"},"788":{"id":"/docs/spec-35","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#specification-map","content":"memory.html"},"789":{"id":"/docs/spec-36","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#specification-map","content":"Arenas, slabs, zero-copy rules, concurrency models"},"790":{"id":"/docs/spec-37","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec#specification-map","content":"database.html"},"791":{"id":"/docs/spec-38","page_id":"/docs/spec","tags":[],"type":"te