emcpy to `out[]` then write"},"992":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-86","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#zero-copy-principles","content":"**Planned:** `writev` scatter if encoding streams"},"993":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-87","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#zero-copy-principles","content":"**Planned:** `sendfile` for static assets; `splice` between sockets for proxy mode; read-only `Slice` into mmap’d config files for the process lifetime."},"994":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-88","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#slice-safety-rules-for-authors","content":"Do not store `Slice.ptr` in global or static variables."},"995":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-89","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#slice-safety-rules-for-authors","content":"Do not return `Slice` from handlers to the runtime except through documented out-parameters filled before return."},"996":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-90","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#slice-safety-rules-for-authors","content":"Treat `ctx->body` as valid only for the synchronous handler call."},"997":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-91","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#slice-safety-rules-for-authors","content":"Assume another pipelined request on the same connection will repurpose `in[]` after the current response is processed."},"998":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-92","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#slice-safety-rules-for-authors","content":"The language does not enforce borrow checking. **Planned** `@safe` mode would compile-time track `Slice` scopes; 0.1 relies on discipline and short arenas."},"999":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-93","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#concurrency-and-memory","content":"**Model A (0.1):** Single thread—no locks on slots, arenas, or SQLite use flag. `busy_timeout` on SQLite only matters if another process opens the same DB file."},"1000":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-94","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#concurrency-and-memory","content":"**Model B (planned):** Workers must not share connection `in[]`/`out[]`. Patterns:"},"1001":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-95","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#concurrency-and-memory","content":"Move request snapshot into owned buffer on handoff"},"1002":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-96","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#concurrency-and-memory","content":"Per-worker arena pools to avoid cross-thread bump allocators"},"1003":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-97","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#concurrency-and-memory","content":"Reference-counted immutable response bodies for cache hits"},"1004":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-98","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#concurrency-and-memory","content":"**Read-copy-update** for read-mostly config (route table, JWT public keys) allows reload without stopping the listener—swap pointer after parsing new table in staging buffer."},"1005":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-99","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#cache-memory-design","content":"In-process LRU for hot keys uses a fixed byte cap from a dedicated slab, not the per-request arena. Eviction is explicit; no GC. Shared **Redis** cache stores serialized blobs; handlers receive copies into arena on hit. See database.html."},"1006":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-100","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#fragmentation-and-long-uptime","content":"Bump arenas eliminate per-request heap fragmentation. Long-lived malloc at startup (routes, SSL) is bounded. **Planned** metrics: arena high-water mark per slot, `out[]` overflow count, slab OOM at accept."},"1007":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-101","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#debugging-memory-bugs","content":"Symptoms and likely causes:"},"1008":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-102","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#debugging-memory-bugs","content":"Symptom"},"1009":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-103","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#debugging-memory-bugs","content":"Likely cause"},"1010":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-104","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#debugging-memory-bugs","content":"Garbage JSON"},"1011":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-105","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#debugging-memory-bugs","content":"`Slice` into freed arena"},"1012":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-106","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#debugging-memory-bugs","content":"Intermittent 500 on large names"},"1013":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-107","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#debugging-memory-bugs","content":"Arena exhaustion"},"1014":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-108","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#debugging-memory-bugs","content":"Crash after DELETE"},"1015":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-109","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#debugging-memory-bugs","content":"Use-after-free on stored `Slice`"},"1016":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-110","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#debugging-memory-bugs","content":"TLS memory growth"},"1017":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-111","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#debugging-memory-bugs","content":"Missing `SSL_free` on error paths"},"1018":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-112","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#debugging-memory-bugs","content":"AddressSanitizer builds of the runtime are recommended for contributors; production binaries trade ASan for speed."},"1019":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-113","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#relation-to-machine-backend","content":"Native ELF programs use the stack and registers only—no arena. Teaching syscalls without libc malloc reinforces the same **explicit lifetime** mindset as the HTTP server."},"1020":{"id":"/docs/spec/memory-114","page_id":"/docs/spec/memory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/memory#relation-to-machine-backend","content":"See boundary.html for ABI types and production.html for capacity planning from slot and buffer sizes."},"1021":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","type":"page","content":"Networking and transport","breadcrumbs":["CForge","Specification"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/networking"},"1022":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-0","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/networking#tcp-server-model","content":"TCP server model"},"1023":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-1","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/networking#read-and-write-semantics","content":"Read and write semantics"},"1024":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-2","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/networking#epoll-user-data-encoding","content":"epoll user-data encoding"},"1025":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-3","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"UDP (design)"},"1026":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-4","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/networking#tls-as-transport","content":"TLS as transport"},"1027":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-5","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/networking#addressing-and-bind-policy","content":"Addressing and bind policy"},"1028":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-6","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/networking#connection-lifecycle-diagram","content":"Connection lifecycle diagram"},"1029":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-7","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/networking#kernel-alternatives-roadmap","content":"Kernel alternatives (roadmap)"},"1030":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-8","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/networking#observability-hooks","content":"Observability hooks"},"1031":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-9","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/spec/networking#failure-matrix","content":"Failure matrix"},"1032":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-10","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking","content":"CForge’s reference server is built on **Linux BSD sockets** and **edge-triggered readiness** via `epoll`. This document specifies transport behavior for the shipped users service and the broader ecosystem design for UDP, connection tuning, TLS as a transport adapter, and future kernel interfaces."},"1033":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-11","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#tcp-server-model","content":"**Shipped (0.1):** One OS thread owns one `epoll` instance. Listen sockets for plain HTTP and optional TLS are registered with distinct user-data tags. Accepted connections become non-blocking (`accept4` with `SOCK_NONBLOCK | SOCK_CLOEXEC`), with `TCP_NODELAY` and `SO_KEEPALIVE` enabled."},"1034":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-12","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#tcp-server-model","content":"Connection state lives in a **fixed slot table** sized by `CFORGE_MAX_CONNS` (default 128, clamped 1–4096 via environment). Each slot tracks:"},"1035":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-13","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#tcp-server-model","content":"File descriptor and optional `SSL *`"},"1036":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-14","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#tcp-server-model","content":"Read buffer cursor (`in_off`, `in_len`) over a preallocated `in[]` slab"},"1037":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-15","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#tcp-server-model","content":"Write state over `out[]`"},"1038":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-16","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#tcp-server-model","content":"Last activity timestamp for idle close"},"1039":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-17","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#tcp-server-model","content":"Epoll interest mask (`EPOLLIN`, `EPOLLOUT`)"},"1040":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-18","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#tcp-server-model","content":"When all slots are busy, listen sockets are **removed from epoll** so the kernel backlog absorbs pressure (`accept_paused` metric). This is deliberate backpressure: the process does not accept fds it cannot service."},"1041":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-19","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#read-and-write-semantics","content":"Reads append to `in[]` until `EAGAIN`. Partial HTTP requests stay in place; the parser returns “need more bytes” without consuming incomplete data. When the user read buffer is full, `EPOLLIN` is dropped until the handler consumes or rejects the request—preventing busy loops on slow clients."},"1042":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-20","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#read-and-write-semantics","content":"Writes buffer the full HTTP response in `out[]` before the first `write` or `SSL_write`. If the syscall returns `EAGAIN`, `EPOLLOUT` is armed and the event loop resumes when the socket is writable. `SIGPIPE` is ignored; closed peers surface as `EPIPE` and trigger slot teardown."},"1043":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-21","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#read-and-write-semantics","content":"Idle connections are scanned on `epoll_wait` timeout (approximately 500 ms, or half of `CFORGE_IDLE_MS` when under one second). Slots exceeding the idle budget close regardless of keep-alive negotiation—this doubles as slow-client protection for half-sent headers."},"1044":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-22","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#epoll-user-data-encoding","content":"**Shipped (0.1)** uses small integer cookies in `epoll_event.data.u64`:"},"1045":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-23","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#epoll-user-data-encoding","content":"Cookie"},"1046":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-24","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#epoll-user-data-encoding","content":"Source"},"1047":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-25","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#epoll-user-data-encoding","content":"`1`"},"1048":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-26","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#epoll-user-data-encoding","content":"`eventfd` for shutdown (`SIGTERM` / `SIGINT`)"},"1049":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-27","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#epoll-user-data-encoding","content":"`2`"},"1050":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-28","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#epoll-user-data-encoding","content":"HTTP listen socket"},"1051":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-29","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#epoll-user-data-encoding","content":"`3`"},"1052":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-30","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#epoll-user-data-encoding","content":"TLS listen socket"},"1053":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-31","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#epoll-user-data-encoding","content":"`10 + index`"},"1054":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-32","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#epoll-user-data-encoding","content":"Connection slot `index`"},"1055":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-33","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#epoll-user-data-encoding","content":"Signal handlers only set a flag and write eight bytes to the eventfd; they do not allocate. Shutdown closes listeners first, marks in-flight connections for close-after-response, then frees global slabs when `active_connections` reaches zero."},"1056":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-34","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#epoll-user-data-encoding","content":"**Planned:** Per-listener load metrics, `EPOLLONESHOT` for accept thundering herds on multi-listener deployments, and optional `SO_REUSEPORT` fan-out across worker processes."},"1057":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-35","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"Release 0.1 does not expose UDP in the runtime API. The ecosystem design includes:"},"1058":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-36","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"Use case"},"1059":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-37","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"API shape"},"1060":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-38","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"Notes"},"1061":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-39","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"DNS resolution"},"1062":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-40","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"Blocking `getaddrinfo` off hot path"},"1063":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-41","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"Cached in startup or worker thread"},"1064":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-42","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"QUIC / HTTP/3"},"1065":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-43","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"UDP socket + userspace stack"},"1066":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-44","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"Separate from epoll HTTP/1 loop initially"},"1067":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-45","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"Metrics push"},"1068":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-46","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"Connected UDP to collector"},"1069":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-47","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"Fire-and-forget with drop counter"},"1070":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-48","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"Game / RTC"},"1071":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-49","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"Dedicated reactor thread"},"1072":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-50","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"Not mixed with HTTP slot table"},"1073":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-51","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#udp-design","content":"UDP endpoints would register parallel epoll entries with the same slot discipline or a smaller datagram ring buffer to avoid per-packet malloc."},"1074":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-52","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#tls-as-transport","content":"TLS terminates in the runtime before bytes are interpreted as HTTP. **Shipped (0.1):** OpenSSL drives `SSL_accept`, `SSL_read`, `SSL_write` on the connection slot. Plaintext HTTP still lands in `in[]`; ciphertext never escapes to handlers."},"1075":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-53","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#tls-as-transport","content":"Context configuration:"},"1076":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-54","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#tls-as-transport","content":"TLS 1.3 only (min and max protocol version pinned)"},"1077":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-55","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#tls-as-transport","content":"Renegotiation and compression disabled"},"1078":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-56","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#tls-as-transport","content":"PEM certificate and private key from environment paths"},"1079":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-57","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#tls-as-transport","content":"Handshake failure closes the socket with no HTTP response"},"1080":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-58","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#tls-as-transport","content":"Dual listeners: HTTP on `PORT` (default 8080), HTTPS on `TLS_PORT` (default 8443) when cert and key are set. **Planned:** ALPN for `h2`, session tickets, OCSP stapling, mutual TLS for service-to-service calls."},"1081":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-59","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#addressing-and-bind-policy","content":"`CFORGE_BIND` defaults to `127.0.0.1`. Production guidance: bind loopback behind a reverse proxy unless the deployment model requires direct exposure. IPv6 listener support is **planned** (`getaddrinfo` with `AI_PASSIVE`, separate slot limits per address family)."},"1082":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-60","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#kernel-alternatives-roadmap","content":"API"},"1083":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-61","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#kernel-alternatives-roadmap","content":"When to adopt"},"1084":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-62","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#kernel-alternatives-roadmap","content":"Tradeoff"},"1085":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-63","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#kernel-alternatives-roadmap","content":"`epoll`"},"1086":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-64","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/spec/networking#kernel-alternatives-roadmap","content":"Default single-thread server"},"1087":{"id":"/docs/spec/networking-65","page_id":"/docs/spec/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/d